Feature 3 — Verify coverage. A lock whose budget is entirely Swift files must refuse to activate with a verifyCommand that only runs TypeScript checks (and vice versa). Check that the verify command plausibly covers the budget's file types; if not, refuse with a message naming what's missing. Refuse on a confident mismatch, warn when the command is unrecognised, and give the lock a field to declare coverage by hand. Every language in the budget must be covered.